{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1773942393,"nonce":"MdPyX4Z3n+cxQweB7CbSrHJSwq8=","title":"Header restructure: emphasize Chat/Auth/Issues, icons, overflow cleanup","message":"Redesign the top-level tab bar to reflect actual usage priorities now that SDK chats happen inside Mandible.\n\n**Primary tabs** (always visible, prominent):\n- **Chat** (console/sessions) — the main interaction surface\n- **Auth** (auth queue) — merge approval workflow\n- **Issues** (git-bug) — work tracking\n\n**Secondary consideration — Inbox**:\nThe inbox shows agent continuation reminders and auth results. It is more important than overflow tabs but its exact placement is uncertain. Current thinking: keep it as a top-level tab. It should NOT be demoted to overflow — it is too useful for the agent loop workflow. Final placement TBD.\n\n**Demoted to overflow**:\n- **Monitor** → rename to 'Process Monitor'. With SDK chats happening inside the app, Monitor is no longer the primary chat surface. It still has value for tracking running processes (PTY sessions, Zellij-based workflows) but should not occupy prime tab real estate. Note: SDK chats are not persistent processes — each user message spawns a transient process — so the monitor's process-centric model doesn't map cleanly to SDK sessions. Address this when implementing.\n- **History** → could become a sub-view or barnacle on the Chat tab rather than a standalone top-level tab. The chat log browsing experience is closely related to the active chat surface.\n\n**Icons**:\nReplace (or supplement) tab text labels with icons. Offer a user preference: text-only, icons-only, or both (standard app convention). This is a visual/UX improvement that should ship alongside the restructure.\n\n**Relates to**: 4d38212 (user-configurable tab layout), e7a8bad (tab nav overhaul), 9606a50 (keyboard shortcuts)","files":null}]}